{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_133336_3c7279", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_d8f4177b80a2411ea9e41d63f3a51206; its implications are already incorporated in LABBOOK.\n\nGSE145237 remains a potential PUM-dependent RNA-persistence resource in HEK293, with PMP22 coverage and results unverified—not validation of the acute Schwann-cell NRG1 response. The unbaselined GSE123016 ActD endpoint, GSE159510 PAC-seq and ENCORE binding/steady-state measurements likewise do not establish that mechanism.\n\nOur selectivity findings and reported RBP transcript coverage remain unchanged. Matched Schwann/NRG1 RNA-fate evidence is still an open dependency. No new analysis or follow-up question is needed for this notification.", "tokens": {"input": 6534, "output": 426, "total": 260784, "cache_read": 253824, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 26750, "timestamp": 1791244517162}
